      <!-- Start Content column -->
      <td width="287" align="left" valign="top"><p align="center"><span class="title-link">Nonsense 10 Poster Show</span>
      <p><a href="http://www.nonsensenyc.com/features/postershow/pages/gallerynav.html"><img src="postershow/images/gallerylookers.jpg" width="300" height="400" /></a></a></p>
        <div align="right">photo by <a target="new" href="http://www.nysun.com/blogs/out-and-about/2009/10/what-makes-new-york-new-york-nonsense.html">Amanda Gordon.</a>
        </div>
        <p><a href="http://www.nonsensenyc.com/features/postershow/pages/gallerynav.html">Online gallery</a> with photos by Jenene Chesbrough.<br />
          <a href="http://todseelie.com/nonsensenycparty/" target="_blank">Event
        photos</a> by Tod Seelie.<br />
        <a href="http://www.flickr.com/photos/thefalserabbit/sets/72157622442125409/" target="_blank">The False Rabbit</a> live poster pictures. <br />
        </p>
        
        <p align="center"><br />
          
         
          <img src="../img/rule.gif" width="107" height="41" />
        </p>
        <p>For a brief period in the early 2000s we thought Nonsense could be a sort of magazine with features and interviews about people who did neat stuff in New York. Turns out that magazines require all kinds of work. We interviewed a few people, we typed out a few transcripts, and then we promptly put away the idea for good. Here are the features:<br />
          <br />
          <a href="http://www.nonsensenyc.com/features/rubulad.html">Rubulad's Chris Thomas and Sari Rubinstein.</a><br />
          <br />
          <a href="http://www.nonsensenyc.com/features/dumboluna.html">Dumboluna.</a><br />
          <br />
          <a href="http://www.nonsensenyc.com/features/politi_int.html">Trash Worship's Roland Politi.</a><br />
          <br />
      Circus composer Sxip Shirey: <a href="http://www.nonsensenyc.com/features/sxip_int1.html">Part 1,</a> <a href="http://www.nonsensenyc.com/features/sxip_int2.html">Part 2.</a></p></td>
